NO CHANGES WERE MADE. The copy is byte-for-byte, which is checkable rather than
asserted: the file carries its own `body_sha256` over a canonical serialisation
of its content, `sunflower_thresh.obligations.load_snapshot` recomputes and
verifies it on every load, and a test pins the sha256 of the whole file against
the copy the report renderer holds. It is vendored rather than fetched because a
report must be rebuildable later from its own bundle, and a regulatory dataset
resolved at run time would mean it is not.

NOT covered by this licence, and not reproduced here or in the vendored file:

  * The text of any regulation. EU legal texts are available from EUR-Lex under
    its own reuse terms; every record links to the text it was read from rather
    than copying it.
  * ISO/IEC 42001. That is a paid standard. Records referencing it carry the
    control IDENTIFIER and a description of what an auditor looks for, and
    reproduce none of the standard's wording.
